# counter harness. One force call is one RgpotCounter.calculate entry.
# GeometryOptimization LBFGS, CG, and GradientDescent call the spec potential.
# The callback stops at the problem Euclidean force norm, or the noise-aware rule.
# v2 success is under the cap, at that stop, and Hessian index 0.
# LJ38 index removes the six rigid modes. A curvature is negative only below -max(force_norm, 1e-8*||H||_F, 1e-6).
# GeometryOptimization 0.1.6 OptimLBFGS uses the Hager-Zhang initial step. BackTracking linesearch of order 2 and maxstep 0.8 bohr. The iteration ceiling is the force-call cap. The potential is the harness callback. The callback stops at the Euclidean force norm 0.01. Positions are labeled bohr and the energy is labeled hartree, so austrip leaves the spec numbers unchanged.
